<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:59:28Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Pope Leo XIV meets abuse victims in Peru, says Church must make 'amends'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc98d46198b391019db2abcd6bff7198728a10d778df40304b8845c380ba8a97</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:59:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T02:58:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-pope-leo-xiv-meets-abuse-victims-in-peru-says-church-must-make-amends--e6391118a168.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-pope-leo-xiv-meets-abuse-victims-in-peru-says-church-must-make-amends" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV met six victims of clerical abuse in Peru on Thursday, including people linked to the disbanded Sodalitium Christianae Vitae. The US-born pontiff also urged the Catholic Church to make amends to survivors and strengthen protections against abuse as he returned to the country where he served for nearly two decades.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Haitian police retake national stadium from gangs after two years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:305e9158e8b785e21feff09f1dce2b6c027395251ad4dd70aae7dba0e9af38a1</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:59:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T02:01:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-haitian-police-retake-national-stadium-from-gangs-after-two-years--7cf91c32db5c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-haitian-police-retake-national-stadium-from-gangs-after-two-years" /><summary type="html">Haitian security forces regained control of the country's main football stadium on Thursday after two years under gang control, with Salvadoran troops taking over security at the venue. The operation comes as El Salvador deploys 2,000 soldiers to Haiti following an ambush that left four of its troops missing.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>‘Peruvian pope’ Leo XIV comes home to a country that shaped his life and faith through 'hardship'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd4acfb659eea50cd5228bc801bc36bb3ba295a3501f3e4b60b6dd240133346b</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:59:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T23:33:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261112-peruvian-pope-leo-xiv-comes-home-to-a-country-that-shaped-his-life-and-faith-through-hardsh--a8e5eb904c4f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261112-peruvian-pope-leo-xiv-comes-home-to-a-country-that-shaped-his-life-and-faith-through-hardship" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Victor Casallo, Director of the Department of Philosophical and Theological Studies at Antonio Ruiz de Montoya University. Can a Pope shaped by Peru's history of political violence, social inequality and religious activism help a deeply polarized nation heal and rediscover the possibility of dialogue? "We tend to see the other person not as someone who holds a different opinion, but as an enemy." Casallo argues that Pope Leo, the first American-born pontiff's identity cannot be understood through his Chicago origins alone.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>‘Peruvian pope’ Leo XIV comes home to a country that shaped his life and faith through 'hardship'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b338e7dfba4f61db81995603752b871c2e99ddea7dcf65c5822ec26a6fef388d</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:59:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T23:26:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/peruvian-pope-leo-xiv-comes-home-to-a-country-that-shaped-his-life-and-faith-through-hardship--621b97b3a738.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/peruvian-pope-leo-xiv-comes-home-to-a-country-that-shaped-his-life-and-faith-through-hardship" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Victor Casallo, Director of the Department of Philosophical and Theological Studies at Antonio Ruiz de Montoya University. Can a Pope shaped by Peru's history of political violence, social inequality and religious activism help a deeply polarized nation heal and rediscover the possibility of dialogue? "We tend to see the other person not as someone who holds a different opinion, but as an enemy." Casallo argues that Pope Leo, the first American-born pontiff's identity cannot be understood through his Chicago origins alone. His decades of pastoral experience in Peru, amid political instability, terrorism, state violence and profound social inequalities, have shaped a religious outlook rooted in cultural openness, solidarity with the marginalized and an intimate understanding of human suffering.</summary></entry><entry><title>Eight killed, including two children, in New York building collapse</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:71c627a0fab02202b08508ede2c02c8e9e178736c45d65350d201e318f0fa686</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:59:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T22:58:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261112-eight-killed-including-two-children-in-new-york-building-collapse--50be159b0c7c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261112-eight-killed-including-two-children-in-new-york-building-collapse" /><summary type="html">Eight people, including two children, were killed when a residential building collapsed into an adjacent construction site in Brooklyn on Wednesday. Firefighters spent hours searching the rubble overnight before declaring the operation over on Thursday, as authorities launched an investigation into the disaster.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>At least five people shot in DC neighbourhood near the White House</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5bc58b1f38e136bf8d2d9e0fe058d325c10ff7372dadb422d1608a6a968a7060</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T16:01:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261112-at-least-five-people-shot-in-dc-neighbourhood-near-the-white-house--c1ab95e70108.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261112-at-least-five-people-shot-in-dc-neighbourhood-near-the-white-house" /><summary type="html">At least one person died after five people were shot early Thursday in a Washington, DC neighbourhood near the White House, police said. A swarm of officers responded to a nearby apartment building where a suspect was barricaded and later shot himself.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth reprimanded at war memorial</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c4c2b7d1de33fc3785fe69f789b3e8c57e4f93154d4771fca1d595f16c568bb2</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:51:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-defense-secretary-pete-hegseth-reprimanded-at-war-memorial--332f267ab309.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-defense-secretary-pete-hegseth-reprimanded-at-war-memorial" /><summary type="html">US Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth, along with his wife and aides, was silenced by a guard on Wednesday at the Tomb of the Unknown Soldier. Hegseth's group was at Arlington National Cemetery for a Veterans Day ceremony when they were reprimanded for laughing and taking pictures in front of the sombre memorial.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang resigns after revelations on extramarital affairs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:976747da3db6afd9e2c781510e1034ba00075f30dc19dd1ca27220b93030b242</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:46:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang-resigns-after-revelations-on-extramarital-affairs--11a6bfe4bbc3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang-resigns-after-revelations-on-extramarital-affairs" /><summary type="html">Jensen Huang resigned as chief executive of AI giant Nvidia on Thursday, November 12, after revelations he had two extramarital affairs, including one with a woman accused of spying for China. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Washington Fraser Jackson and FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert have more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Mississippi elects its first African American to US Senate since Reconstruction</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df94e8c9fc0b446054e5b20cd39c144d8fa8627c32dcc16e021098425e120182</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T14:23:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-mississippi-elects-its-first-african-american-to-us-senate-since-reconstruction--c58f82d3f782.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-mississippi-elects-its-first-african-american-to-us-senate-since-reconstruction" /><summary type="html">Democrat Scott Colom defeated Republican Senator Cindy Hyde-Smith to become Mississippi’s first Black US Senator since Reconstruction. His narrow victory, confirmed on November 11 after prolonged ballot counting, marks a major political shift in the conservative state. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Huang powers and bankrolls AI revolution: Nvidia CEO caught between 'a rock and a very hard place'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78c2246cdace62a21e5e0a54be776ee545fc9249e84929782789313d259d8235</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T14:11:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-he-powers-and-bankrolls-ai-revolution-nvidia-ceo-huang-caught-between-rock-and-a-very-hard---ce288d10e4d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-he-powers-and-bankrolls-ai-revolution-nvidia-ceo-huang-caught-between-rock-and-a-very-hard-place-1" /><summary type="html">Oliver Farry is pleased to welcome Bernard Benhamou, Secretary General of France's Institute of Digital Sovereignty. Benhamou examines the intersection of traditional espionage, geopolitical rivalry and the extraordinary concentration of power within the global AI industry. Discussing allegations surrounding Nvidia's leadership, he describes the chipmaker as "the banker of the global AI system," a striking characterization that captures the company's importance not merely as a semiconductor manufacturer, but as a central actor in the economic and technological infrastructure underpinning the AI boom. "Because humans stay humans." Benhamou identifies one of the central paradoxes of the artificial intelligence revolution: even as technological systems acquire unprecedented strategic and economic importance, the individuals who control them remain susceptible to familiar forms of influence, manipulation and misjudgment.</summary></entry><entry><title>Paraguayans get some savings back after banking collapse disrupted economy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc5541b0f068c127399822b29eb58caa45dbb0c939a394e991a2994758aca566</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T11:24:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-paraguayans-get-some-savings-back-after-banking-collapse-disrupted-economy--3e73b54b4bc5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-paraguayans-get-some-savings-back-after-banking-collapse-disrupted-economy" /><summary type="html">Paraguay's Central Bank said Wednesday, November 11, it had partially returned savings to all eligible Ueno Bank depositors locked out of their accounts when it collapsed last week. The digital bank's takeover on November 3 triggered massive protests across Paraguay and led to the impeachment and arrest of ex-president Santiago Pena, who is linked to Ueno.</summary></entry><entry><title>Scott Colom makes history in Mississippi as first Black senator in more than 140 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a044b0857a4aee36b9241de78079c70d045b8174ece77873100b249c6cdd697</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T10:50:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261112-scott-colom-makes-history-in-mississippi-as-first-black-senator-in-more-than-140-years--225d5e2b56d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261112-scott-colom-makes-history-in-mississippi-as-first-black-senator-in-more-than-140-years" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, November 12: We look at reactions from Spain after the country's first nationwide general strike in 14 years. It comes two weeks before snap general elections. Also: Scott Colom makes history as the first Black senator in Mississippi in 145 years after an epic Senate midterm race finally concluded. Finally, fans of Barça will be able to inter their ashes at Camp Nou as part of a new offer by the club to allow supporters to cheer on the team in the afterlife.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Mississippi Democrat Scott Colom flips US Senate seat in stunning upset</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e141aa378e6e7a8fb8070a0dcfe551aa86edd7301d28c36a18ce93122f1e8f20</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T10:39:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/mississippi-democrat-scott-colom-flips-us-senate-seat-in-stunning-upset--fb56bec12510.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/mississippi-democrat-scott-colom-flips-us-senate-seat-in-stunning-upset" /><summary type="html">In a historic upset, Democrat Scott Colom has won his US Senate race in traditionally conservative Mississippi, networks projected Wednesday, making him the first African American elected to the chamber from the southern state in more than 140 years. Report by Morgan Ayre</summary></entry><entry><title>Who is Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e7f13c2cd51659212be01287181ba2b69df3f340e54dc5114d612c46d6bb30b3</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T07:54:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/who-is-nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang--eb64994727b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/who-is-nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang" /><summary type="html">Nvidia's board met late Wednesday to decide whether to oust CEO ​Jensen Huang, a source familiar with the matter told Reuters, as the world's dominant supplier of AI chips grapples with fallout from reports of two extramarital affairs involving its longtime leader. Report by Jack Pownall and Eliza Herbert.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nvidia board weighs ouster of CEO Jensen Huang amid spy scandal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9dd2cfa734204b27411540d0e8001547583cea8100f8cd15530148b3a76851f5</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T04:05:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261112-nvidia-board-weighs-ouster-of-ceo-jensen-huang-amid-spy-scandal--f5d59a17f8a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261112-nvidia-board-weighs-ouster-of-ceo-jensen-huang-amid-spy-scandal" /><summary type="html">Nvidia's board met late Wednesday to consider removing chief executive Jensen Huang, after reports of two extramarital affairs, including one with an alleged Chinese spy, fuelled a market sell-off and raised questions about the AI chipmaker's leadership.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Paraguay partially refunds Ueno Bank depositors after collapse</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5bb94f4ff522468727e6f946bdc742bf9a1657683a780e01e190ff7e2b63086f</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T03:11:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261112-paraguay-partially-refunds-ueno-bank-depositors-after-collapse--5fcadbef855d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261112-paraguay-partially-refunds-ueno-bank-depositors-after-collapse" /><summary type="html">Paraguay's Central Bank said Wednesday it had partially returned savings to all eligible Ueno Bank depositors, following the lender's collapse last week. The crisis triggered mass protests and the impeachment and arrest of former president Santiago Peña, who is accused of directing government funds to the bank.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Democrat Scott Colom wins historic Senate race in Mississippi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6ca8d4057612b9c1011eabd053378ff35807ee12094185112908552ebfbc96fc</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T23:47:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261111-democrat-scott-colom-wins-historic-senate-race-in-mississippi--af617c105330.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261111-democrat-scott-colom-wins-historic-senate-race-in-mississippi" /><summary type="html">Democrat Scott Colom defeated Republican Senator Cindy Hyde-Smith in Mississippi after a final count on Wednesday, becoming the state's first Black US senator since Reconstruction. His narrow victory adds to the Democrats' midterm gains as President Donald Trump's party suffers a series of defeats.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo XIV returns to second homeland Peru and a nationwide welcome</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35d9524a49a4b51b16c6d15ef5beb756ef39302871f698f0fa836b097670d00b</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T23:43:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261111-pope-leo-xiv-returns-to-second-homeland-peru-to-a-nationwide-welcome--772c1b81a17b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261111-pope-leo-xiv-returns-to-second-homeland-peru-to-a-nationwide-welcome" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV arrived in Peru on Wednesday for the final leg of his South American tour, returning to the country where he spent more than two decades as a missionary and bishop. Thousands gathered to welcome him home as “Padre Robert”, with many hoping his visit will bring attention to the country's poverty, crime and political instability.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Failed state: Haiti has collapsed in a kind of a black hole'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c67edc489a0d933e72eb8a23d311a7390ad2daa3171c912b78e19585751211f6</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T16:38:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/bukele-says-salvadoran-troops-destroyed-gang-hq-in-haiti--a7661e77071f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/bukele-says-salvadoran-troops-destroyed-gang-hq-in-haiti" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Jean Marie Théodat, Author and Head of the Geography Department at Paris 1 Panthéon-Sorbonne University. He describes Haiti as a failed state: "Haiti has collapsed in a kind of a black hole. I mean there is no president, no elections, no chambers of deputies, no senators." Addressing the reported deployment of Salvadoran troops to Haiti, he says “when you are dying, you don't look at the hand that brings help,” explaining why many Haitians may welcome military assistance from Salvadoran President Nayib Bukele despite concerns about his government's authoritarian methods and the uncertain political consequences of foreign intervention. Drawing on a Haitian proverb, he warns that “a goat with several masters can die of thirst while tied up,” underscoring the dangers of poorly coordinated interventions.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil electoral court fines Meta $1.3 MN, sees no deliberate election bias</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:81550c6bb681836937db4a151eb0ed0c17f377c6aa2cc038ee1cd25f65cbdf36</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T16:08:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-electoral-court-fines-meta-1-3-mn-sees-no-deliberate-election-bias--81c14c584e59.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-electoral-court-fines-meta-1-3-mn-sees-no-deliberate-election-bias" /><summary type="html">Jan Onoszko, our correspondent in Rio, has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>US House votes to derail impeachment of Defense Secretary Hegseth</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1899a81f89c1302953125adee976e58cd117a69e0855139b5e4f03f908832dd</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T12:17:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-house-votes-to-derail-impeachment-of-defense-secretary-hegseth--b2d11278e1a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-house-votes-to-derail-impeachment-of-defense-secretary-hegseth" /><summary type="html">Republicans in ​the US House ​of Representatives banded together on Tuesday ​to ‌derail ⁠aneffort to impeach ‌Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth. Fraser Jackson, our correspondant in Washington DC, has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Welcome Home': Peru awaits Pope Leo's emotional 'homecoming'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:385406b15a35fa38ee4c1117beeb9ddb4b15bde2f505494152c1c4670cb6439d</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T11:53:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/welcome-home-peru-awaits-pope-leo-s-emotional-homecoming--c0f157d7b90d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/welcome-home-peru-awaits-pope-leo-s-emotional-homecoming" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo will wrap ​up his visit to Argentina on Wednesday during his 12-day South America tour, with a final event expected to draw millions, before traveling to Peru in an emotional homecoming for the first Peruvian citizen to lead the Catholic Church.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo to end Argentina tour with outdoor mass before Peru 'homecoming'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c710e4984286afa8d501594a2e6b13a802b324f29d83468fdcc290df844592cd</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T10:50:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261111-pope-leo-to-end-argentina-tour-with-large-outdoor-mass-before-emotional-peru-homecoming--6a3146ea450a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261111-pope-leo-to-end-argentina-tour-with-large-outdoor-mass-before-emotional-peru-homecoming" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo will conclude his three-day visit to Argentina Wednesday with an outdoor mass expected to draw millions before continuing his tour of South America by travelling to Peru, where he once served as a missionary. The pontiff plans to deliver a speech in front of Peruvian President Keiko Fujimori, whose election earlier this year was marred ‌by fraud accusations and vote-counting delays.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Nayib Bukele says Salvadoran troops destroyed gang HQ in Haiti</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c7a11fe77612eb366404ea4745f54a246126a68207ef98dda8ec03dca548277c</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T09:58:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nayib-bukele-says-salvadoran-troops-destroyed-gang-hq-in-haiti--b10ad102843e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nayib-bukele-says-salvadoran-troops-destroyed-gang-hq-in-haiti" /><summary type="html">President Nayib Bukele said Tuesday that Salvadoran troops deployed to Haiti had destroyed the headquarters of one of the Caribbean nation's most powerful gangs.Bukele has deployed more than 2,000 soldiers to Haiti since late October, after four Salvadoran troops went missing in the country.</summary></entry><entry><title>House Republicans quash effort to impeach Defense Secretary Hegseth</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:58b9176b122f0b664600f7f6aa9c592f27418078f7793a164c6ec766e421b5c7</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T09:55:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/house-republicans-quash-effort-to-impeach-defense-secretary-hegseth--ff1ba7de638a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/house-republicans-quash-effort-to-impeach-defense-secretary-hegseth" /><summary type="html">Rochelle Ferguson Bouyahi, our international affairs editor, has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>UK authorities arrest US soldier suspected of spying for Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18ed4641881563bee45313df61014c2241a26d3545f8b6366b88ac91b1f97bf1</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T09:41:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/uk-authorities-arrests-us-soldier-suspected-of-spying-for-russia--305fec5257b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/uk-authorities-arrests-us-soldier-suspected-of-spying-for-russia" /><summary type="html">A member of the US army suspected of spying for Russia was arrested in Britain on Tuesday, London police said, following an investigation with support from the American military and law enforcement.</summary></entry><entry><title>Want to live on the moon? NASA opens recruitment for Artemis programme</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d1ac5dbbf9c7833eb4209b34cb86eda26ca903e12c4df431db3126e6f32704cc</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T08:42:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/want-to-live-moon-nasa-opens-recruitment-for-artemis-programme--b459f89a5e4c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/want-to-live-moon-nasa-opens-recruitment-for-artemis-programme" /><summary type="html">NASA is expanding its astronaut corps for the first time in two years. As the US space agency grows its Artemis programme, recruitment is in progress for a brand-new class of space explorers who will train to "live and work beyond Earth".</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US House blocks bid to impeach Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:432c3e5f85c4a9e0f994af95d7ac316177f87ff5f1d1bfc7be2134712fb1df08</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T08:33:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261111-us-house-blocks-bid-to-impeach-defense-secretary-pete-hegseth--af1cac87fbe3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261111-us-house-blocks-bid-to-impeach-defense-secretary-pete-hegseth" /><summary type="html">The US House of Representatives turned aside a resolution to impeach Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth on Tuesday, halting an effort to remove the Pentagon chief for his conduct in office and his handling of the war in Iran. Story by Jack Pownall.</summary></entry><entry><title>Haiti's PM praises Bukele after Salvadoran troops help destroy gang headquarters</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:50b05613c0a64c0e8054717eaab7c48b32d37a497212309b8bd2c4acfa496723</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T01:41:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261111-haiti-pm-bukele-salvadoran-troops-gang-headquarters--87db38cfc001.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261111-haiti-pm-bukele-salvadoran-troops-gang-headquarters" /><summary type="html">Haitian Prime Minister Alix Didier Fils-Aimé praised Salvadoran President Nayib Bukele on Tuesday after Salvadoran troops aided in the destruction a suspected gang leader’s home near Port-au-Prince. Bukele’s deployment of more than 2,000 soldiers following four Salvadoran troops’ disappearance has raised concerns over rules of engagement and coordination with a UN-backed force combating Haiti’s gangs.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump ally Jim Jordan elected House Republican leader after midterm defeat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c0504489f6a131d517984753eeef1930c0919cff6903149f58ae1612c8ace9cd</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T22:42:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261110-trump-jim-jordan-elected-house-republican-leader-midterm-defeat--88636c0967f2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261110-trump-jim-jordan-elected-house-republican-leader-midterm-defeat" /><summary type="html">Congressman Jim Jordan, a hardline ally of President Donald Trump, was elected House Republican leader on Tuesday, defeating Steve Scalise 106-73 in a secret ballot, US media reported. He replaces Mike Johnson after Republicans lost both chambers of Congress in last week’s midterm elections and will lead the party’s opposition.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry></feed>
